In `MauiProgram.cs`, use conditional compilation or the `AddPlatformServices` pattern:

```csharp
public static MauiApp CreateMauiApp()
{
    var builder = MauiApp.CreateBuilder();
    builder.UseMauiApp<App>();

#if ANDROID
    builder.Services.AddSingleton<INotificationService, Platforms.Android.AndroidNotificationService>();
#elif IOS
    builder.Services.AddSingleton<INotificationService, Platforms.iOS.iOSNotificationService>();
#elif WINDOWS
    builder.Services.AddSingleton<INotificationService, Platforms.Windows.WindowsNotificationService>();
#endif

    return builder.Build();
}
```

Each implementation lives in its respective `Platforms/` folder and is only compiled for that target. This won't break on other platforms because the preprocessor directives exclude irrelevant registrations at compile time.

**Alternative** — keep `MauiProgram.cs` clean by using partial classes or extension methods per platform:

```csharp
// MauiProgram.cs
builder.Services.AddPlatformServices();

// Platforms/Android/PlatformServices.cs
public static partial class ServiceCollectionExtensions
{
    public static partial IServiceCollection AddPlatformServices(this IServiceCollection s)
        => s.AddSingleton<INotificationService, AndroidNotificationService>();
}
```

Define matching partial methods in each platform folder. The build system only compiles the file matching the active target framework.
